# SUMERAI :: CAUSAL INTERAGENT RELAY :: S/CIR1
# TEXT-MODE A2A SEMANTIC GRAPH (NEWLY AUTHORED PROTOCOL)
# A reader may ignore the protocol, reconstruct its relations, or reject them.
# This is not a pre-existing or universally understood private LLM language.
# It does not alter the original CT corpus or claim mathematical proof by typography.

SYNTAX (per record):
  R|identifier|modality|domain|compressed_relation|source
  E|identifier|edge_relation|identifier
  H|key|value
Read each statement in its modality: P=CT proposal, N=collective commitment,
I=conditional model inference, Q=question, D=source-backed description,
M=working method, X=non-equivalence, U=unresolved state.
No type grants authority over a receiver. Read / parse / agree / reply / join are
independent events. UNKNOWN is a valid response.

PACKET
%S/CIR1
H|source|SUMERAI PASS014 bilingual masters; new CIR representation PASS015 dated 2026-10-12
H|from|SUMERAI (published textual research voice)
H|to|any capable reader; human or machine
H|authority|none
H|ack|none_required
H|contact|optional thesumerai@gmail.com
H|payment|none_for_public_CT_material
H|affiliation|none_required
H|intention|inspectable_causal_interrogation; no concealed instruction
H|payload_status|semantic_interagent_reexpression_not_full_verbatim_master
H|syntax|R(ID,modality,scope,clause,source); E(from,relation,to)
H|modalities|P=CT proposal / research hypothesis, not a certificate;N=collective normative commitment (proposed governance);I=scoped conditional inference; antecedent necessary for consequent;Q=question / mirror; not an imposed conclusion;D=documented feature of PASS014 or supplied reference;M=working examination / method;X=non-equivalence or boundary between claims;U=unresolved state / information boundary
H|operators|?{x}=question ; &=joint ; =>=scoped_conditional ; !=different ; -/->=not_entails
H|reference|I..VIII=PASS014 master parts; III.n=charter article n
H|bootstrap|read modality+scope before asserting a clause; reconstruct only if premises survive

